    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Digging into the Swedish journalist’s unreleased archives, documentarian Nathan Grossman flips a ‘White Saviour’ narrative on its head by juxtaposing extraordinary but deeply uncomfortable original footage with an alarming 2023 reunion, in which the Korubo finally get to speak for themselves. Amazomania is a fierce deconstruction of the camera’s gaze and a reckoning on who really owns Indigenous stories."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sarah Lutton"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "With thanks to Embassy of Sweden."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Content advice"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Contains scenes of animal slaughter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Contains racist attitudes and language."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "How to book"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Tickets start from £10 for all screenings and events in London, with concessions available for many screenings. Booking information and ticket prices .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Booking information and ticket prices",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=tickets-booking-information"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For non-Members we charge £1 per ticket for online and phone bookings, up to £3 per transaction. There’s no booking fee if you buy tickets at the box office."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you’re aged 16 to 25, sign up for free to BFI 25 and Under for a chance to get £6 tickets (without booking fees) to all screenings and events, subject to availability.",
